# La'An Noonien-Singh, Security's "Whenever you attack while creatures you control have total power 8 or greater, target
# creature can't block this turn" (CR 508.3d, 603.4, 509.1b). On turn 5 La'An (4) and Bonebreaker Giant (4) attack for
# exactly 8 power, so the trigger happens; Bot2's Llanowar Elves, chosen, may not block the Giant (8 damage: Bot2 at 12).
# On turn 7 only the Giant attacks, but La'An still counts - it is the creatures you control, attacking or not, that total
# 8 - so it triggers again; Bot1 targets La'An herself, and the same Elves block the Giant: the turn-5 effect has ended
# (CR 514.2), and the 1/1 dies to the 4/4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
La'An Noonien-Singh, Security
Bonebreaker Giant
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x18

